    {
      "id": 158601,
      "name": "dpt",
      "username": "dpt",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-02T19:08:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Bunston\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bunston/48/1939_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Bunston:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, if you discard an environment card that doesn't have a keyword (like Temporal Event), then you could destroy any hero character card except Sky-Scraper, as the statement \"Heroes and [insert environment card here] share a keyword\" is vacuously true.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I disagree here. There is no keyword that the two cards share. On the other hand, if the power said \"destroy a card that has all the keywords of the revealed card\", THEN it would be vacuously true.</p>\n<p>(I think about vacuous conditions all the time in my day job!)</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:38:45.084Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
