      "id": 158602,
      "name": "The Burning Stickman",
      "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-02T19:25:13.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Bunston wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Also, if you discard an environment card that doesn't have a keyword (like Temporal Event), then you could destroy any hero character card except Sky-Scraper, as the statement \"Heroes and [insert environment card here] share a keyword\" is vacuously true.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI disagree here. There is no keyword that the two cards share.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's how Experiment works in the video game – I once experimented on Wagner Mars Base, which revealed two of the same card (Villainous Weaponry), and discarded both because they had no keywords to share.</p>",
