      "created_at": "2016-02-02T19:29:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>dpt wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Bunston wrote:<br><blockquote>Also, if you discard an environment card that doesn't have a keyword (like Temporal Event), then you could destroy any hero character card except Sky-Scraper, as the statement \"Heroes and [insert environment card here] share a keyword\" is vacuously true.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nI disagree here. There is no keyword that the two cards share.\n</blockquote></div>\nThat's how Experiment works in the video game -- I once experimented on Wagner Mars Base, which revealed two of the same card (Villainous Weaponry), and discarded both because they had no keywords to share.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Sounds like a bug to me. A card without keywords shouldnt have any keywords to share to trigger the effect.</p>",
